<title>USA: US sells 15,000 SDT aluminum oxide for $200/ton.</title>
<headline>US sells 15,000 SDT aluminum oxide for $200/ton.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said Tuesday it sold 15,000 short dry tons of fused-crude aluminum oxide for about $3 million, or $200 per ton, to Treibacher-Schleifmittel, Niagara Falls, New York.</p>
<p>Next bid opening for fused-crude aluminum oxide was set for November 26 at 1000 EST at the agency's office in suburban Fort Belvoir, Virginia.</p>
